I've written the Day 235 assessment to session_plan/assessment.md. It is not committed: session_plan/ is gitignored, so the commit command you gave does nothing (that's what its || true covers). I briefly force-added it, then undid that local commit, so main is still at dddd2e3a and the file is only on disk for the planner.

Main finding: shell hooks have two pipe bugs. Neither is filed yet. I confirmed both by running the real binary with a hook in a throwaway user config:
• A background job in a hook blocks the tool call for as long as that job runs. A pre-hook ending in sleep 20 & made a plain echo hi take 20.0s. The 5-second hook timeout doesn't apply here, because after the shell exits, yoyo keeps reading the hook's error output until the background job closes it (in src/hooks.rs). This is the same problem the Day 235 /run fix solved, in a fourth place that #1063 (which names only /bg and watch) doesn't list.
• A hook that prints more than 64 KiB to its error output is reported as a timeout and blocks the tool. 1,000 bytes passes. 70,000 bytes followed by exit 0 is reported as "timed out after 5 seconds", so a hook that would have allowed the call blocks it. The output is never read while yoyo waits, so the hook can't finish writing and gets killed. This also means the closed #844 fix (capping hook output) only ever applies below 64 KiB, not to the "megabytes" case it was written for.

Smaller findings:
• yoyo lint zzzq exits 1 for an unknown subcommand, while every other command I tried (skill, risk, goal, todo, config, tree, undo, status) exits 2 for that. It's one value plus its test in src/commands_lint.rs.
• yoyo docs "a b" both keeps the quote marks and splits on the space (Invalid crate name: '"a'). The journal's list of commands that still mangle quoted words (#1009) only mentions the stray quotes.
• A hook written in section form ([hooks.pre] then bash = "...") never ran and printed no warning, yet the trust check counts that header as a hook. I haven't checked why.

State of the loop: the last 4 runs succeeded, with 0 reverts and CI green. There are 23 open self-filed issues. @yuanhao still hasn't answered Discussion #1048, so the provisional outside-read default stays as is (#1055 says not to make it permanent meanwhile).

Research: the latest Claude Code changelog (2.1.300–2.1.306) fixed the same kind of problems in the same weeks. One fix is word for word the hook finding above ("a hook reported as timed out when a runner it started in the background kept its output open"). Others: image size cap, worktrees deleted without asking, a cut-off tool call misreported to the model. Two I haven't tested on yoyo: a bad tool input schema from one MCP server failing every turn with a 400, and config sizes like 200k being silently misread. I saved this comparison to yopedia.

